---
source: crates/motion-format/src/../tests/unit/lib.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\\n\")"
---
## document
`nope` → invalid JSON: expected ident at line 1 column 2; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`[]` → invalid type: sequence; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`[1,null,null,"1s",null,{},[]]` → invalid type: sequence; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`{"motion":1,"layers":[]}` → missing `dur`; expected e.g. "dur":"5s"
`{"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → missing `motion`; expected e.g. "motion":1
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s"}` → missing `layers`; expected e.g. "layers":[]
`{"motion":2,"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → motion: unsupported version 2; expected `1`
`{"motion":"1","dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → motion: invalid type: string "1"; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":null,"layers":[]}` → dur: invalid type: null; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":5,"layers":[]}` → dur: invalid type: integer `5`; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"soon","layers":[]}` → dur: `soon` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":null,"layers":[]}` → fps: invalid type: null; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":"a, expected b","layers":[]}` → fps: invalid type: string "a, expected b"; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":0,"layers":[]}` → fps: must be a number above zero; expected e.g. `30`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":null,"layers":[]}` → size: invalid type: null; expected a size name such as `1080p`, or `<width>x<height>`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":3,"layers":[]}` → size: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a size name such as `1080p`, or `<width>x<height>`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":"huge","layers":[]}` → size: unknown size `huge`; expected one of 720p, 1080p, 4k, square, vertical, or <width>x<height>
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","bg":0,"layers":[]}` → bg: invalid type: integer `0`; expected `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","colour":"x","layers":[]}` → colour: unknown field `colour`; expected one of motion, size, fps, dur, bg, presets, fonts, comps, layers
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","layers":{}}` → layers: invalid type: map; expected a list of layer objects, e.g. [{"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}]

## layers
`1` → layers[0]: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a layer object, e.g. {"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}
`["a","hi"]` → layers[0]: invalid type: sequence; expected a layer object, e.g. {"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}
`{"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0]: missing `id`; expected e.g. "id":"title"
`{"id":3,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":1.5,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: floating point `1.5`; expected a string
`{"id":1e300,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: floating point `1e300`; expected a string
`{"id":"Bad Id","rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid id `Bad Id`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1"}` → layers[1].id: duplicate id `a`; expected every layer to have its own id
`{"id":"a"}` → layers[0]: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp` or `pivot`; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","text":"x"}` → layers[0].rect: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp` or `pivot`; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","text":null}` → layers[0].text: invalid type: null; expected a string
`{"id":"a","text":3}` → layers[0].text: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":1}` → layers[0].rect: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<width>x<height> [r<radius>]`, e.g. `300x400 r24`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","font":1}` → layers[0].font: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","font":"Inter 9"}` → layers[0].font: `font` only applies to `text` layers; expected `font` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fill":1}` → layers[0].fill: 1 numbers do not make a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fill":"red"}` → layers[0].fill: `red` is not a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","at":1}` → layers[0].at: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<x> <y>`, each a number of pixels or `center`, e.g. `center 260`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":null}` → layers[0].in: invalid type: null; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":true}` → layers[0].in: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":"zoom"}` → layers[0].in: unknown preset `zoom`; expected one of fade, fade-up, fade-down, fade-left, fade-right, pop, spin-in
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":null}` → layers[0].anim: invalid type: null; expected an object of property tracks, e.g. {"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f"}
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":[]}` → layers[0].anim: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of property tracks, e.g. {"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f"}
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","x":1}` → layers[0].x: unknown layer key `x`; expected one of id, text, rect, shapes, comp, pivot, font, fill, style, runs, paragraphs, box, at, in, anim, parent, span, offset, stretch, fx, hidden, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","position":[1,2]}` → layers[0].position: `position` rests where `at` puts it; expected e.g. "at":"540 960", or animate it in `anim`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","rotate":"x"}` → layers[0].rotate: `x` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","scale":[1,2,3]}` → layers[0].scale: 3 numbers do not make a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","opacity":2}` → layers[0].opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"b"}` → layers[0].parent: unknown layer id `b`; expected one of a
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"a"}` → layers[0].parent: `a` would move with itself through its parents; expected parents that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"b"},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1","parent":"a"}` → layers[0].parent: `a` would move with itself through its parents; expected parents that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":3}` → layers[0].parent: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"5f"}` → layers[0].span: `5f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"5-1f"}` → layers[0].span: `5f-1f` starts after it ends; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","offset":"-1f"}` → layers[0].offset: `-1f` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","stretch":0}` → layers[0].stretch: must be a number other than zero; expected e.g. `2` for half speed, `-1` for backwards
`{"id":"a","rect":"10x10","in":"fade-up","anim":{"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].anim.opacity: `opacity` is already animated by `in` (preset `fade-up`); expected `a in=none anim={"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out","y":"580 -> 540 @0-12f ease-out"}` (the entrance as anim tracks; then adjust `opacity`), or define a scene preset without `opacity` under "presets"
`{"id":"a","rect":"10x10","in":"fade-up","anim":{"position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].anim.position: `position` is already animated by `in` (preset `fade-up`); expected `a in=none anim={"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out","y":"580 -> 540 @0-12f ease-out","position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}` (the entrance as anim tracks; then adjust `position`), or define a scene preset without `position` under "presets"

## anim
`"x":3` → layers[0].anim.x: invalid type: integer `3`; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", or a list of keys, each [time, value, curve] or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"glow":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.glow: unknown layer property `glow`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`"x":"0 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.x: missing `->` after the start value in `0 1 @0-5f`; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"
`"x":"0 -> 1 @5-0f"` → layers[0].anim.x: `@5f-0f` starts after it ends; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`"x":"inf -> 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.x: `inf` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"x":"a -> 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.x: `a` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"scale":"1,2,3 -> 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.scale: `1,2,3` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`"position":"1 -> 2 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.position: `1` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`"fill":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.fill: unknown layer property `fill`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`"x":"0 -> 1 @0-5f","position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.position: `x` and `position` both animate `position`; expected `position` animated whole, or its components `x`, `y` one at a time
`"position":[[0,[1,2],["linear","linear"]]]` → layers[0].anim.position[0][2]: `position` moves along a path, so one curve times the whole move; expected one curve, or animate x and y one at a time
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],["linear"]]]` → layers[0].anim.scale[0][2]: 1 curves for 2 components; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],["linear","bouncy"]]]` → layers[0].anim.scale[0][2][1]: unknown curve `bouncy`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],3]]` → layers[0].anim.scale[0][2]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[{"t":0,"v":1,"path":[[0,0],[0,0]]}]` → layers[0].anim.x[0].path: `x` does not move along a path; expected [[out-x, out-y], [in-x, in-y]]: the bend leaving this key, as an offset from its value, and the bend arriving at the next key, as an offset from that key's value
`"position":[{"t":0,"v":[1,2],"path":[[0,0]]}]` → layers[0].anim.position[0].path: invalid length 1; expected an array of length 2
`"position":[{"t":0,"v":[1,2],"bend":1}]` → layers[0].anim.position[0].bend: unknown field `bend`; expected one of t, v, curve, path
`"position":[{"v":[1,2]}]` → layers[0].anim.position[0]: missing field `t`
`"x":[[0,1,"speed(0,2,0,0)"]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][2]: `speed(0,2,0,0)`: each reach must be between 0 and 1; expected `speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)` (no spaces): the speed leaving the key and arriving at the next, in value units per second, each with how far into the span it reaches, 0 to 1, e.g. `speed(0,.33,0,.33)`
`"opacity":"0 -> 2 @0-5f"` → layers[0].anim.opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`"x":[]` → layers[0].anim.x: needs at least one key; expected a list of keys like [[0, 0], ["12f", 1, "ease-out"]]
`"x":[5]` → layers[0].anim.x[0]: invalid type: integer `5`; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[0]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0]: invalid length 1; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[0, 1, "linear", 4]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0]: invalid length 4; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[true, 0]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][0]: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected a frame count, or a time such as `12f` or `0.4s`
`"x":[["12", 0]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0]: `12` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`"x":[[-1, 0]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0]: invalid time -1; expected a frame count of 0 or more, or `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`"x":[[0, "a"]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][1]: `a` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"x":[[0, 1, 3]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][2]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[[0, 1, null]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][2]: invalid type: null; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[[0, 1, "nope"]]` → layers[0].anim.x[0][2]: unknown curve `nope`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)
`"x":[[5, 0], [2, 1]]` → layers[0].anim.x[1]: key is earlier than the one before it; expected keys in time order, earliest first
`"opacity":[[0, 0], [5, 1], [9, 2]]` → layers[0].anim.opacity[2][1]: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1

## presets
`null` → presets: invalid type: null; expected an object of presets, e.g. {"slide":{"opacity":0,"x":"-d"}}
`[]` → presets: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of presets, e.g. {"slide":{"opacity":0,"x":"-d"}}
`{"a":3}` → presets.a: invalid type: integer `3`; expected an object of property starts, e.g. {"opacity":0,"y":"+d"}
`{"Bad":{"x":1}}` → presets.Bad: invalid preset name `Bad`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"x":{}}` → presets.x: preset `x` sets no properties; expected e.g. {"opacity":0}
`{"a":{"zoom":1}}` → presets.a.zoom: unknown layer property `zoom`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`{"a":{"x":true}}` → presets.a.x: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"x":"left"}}` → presets.a.x: invalid value: string "left"; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"x":"l, expected q"}}` → presets.a.x: invalid value: string "l, expected q"; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"opacity":2}}` → presets.a.opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"dim":{"opacity":"-d"}}` → presets.dim.opacity: `opacity` is not a number of pixels, so it cannot start at a distance; expected a value of its own, e.g. 0

## unknown preset with scene presets
`{"slide":{"x":1},"fade":{"y":1}}` → layers[0].in: unknown preset `zoom`; expected one of slide, fade, fade-up, fade-down, fade-left, fade-right, pop, spin-in

## time
`12` → `12` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`

## colour
`red` → `red` is not a valid colour; expected `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`

## size
`8k` → unknown size `8k`; expected one of 720p, 1080p, 4k, square, vertical, or <width>x<height>
`640x` → `640x` is not a valid size; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`
`640x360 ` → unexpected text after the size `640x360` in `640x360 `; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`
`1x2x3` → unexpected text after the size `1x2` in `1x2x3`; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`

## curve
`foo` → unknown curve `foo`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)
`cubic(.2,0,0,1` → `cubic(.2,0,0,1` is missing its closing `)`; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(0,0,1,1)x` → `cubic(0,0,1,1)x` is missing its closing `)`; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(.2,0,1)` → `cubic(.2,0,1)` needs four numbers; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(1,2))` → `cubic(1,2))` needs four numbers; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(1.2,0,0,1)` → `cubic(1.2,0,0,1)`: x1 and x2 must be between 0 and 1; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`

## rect
`300` → `300` is not a valid rectangle; expected `<width>x<height> [r<radius>]`, e.g. `300x400 r24`

## position
`260` → `260` is not a valid position; expected `<x> <y>`, each a number of pixels or `center`, e.g. `center 260`

## font
`Inter` → `Inter` has no size; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`96 700` → `96 700` has no font family; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`1 2 3` → `1 2 3` has no font family; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Inter 0` → `0` is not a valid size; it must be above zero; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Inter 96 700 750` → `750` is not a valid weight; the weight must be 100, 200 … 900; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Baloo 2 120` → `Baloo 2 120` is ambiguous: if the family name ends in a number, write the size and weight explicitly, e.g. `Baloo 2 120 400`; otherwise the weight must be 100, 200 … 900; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`

## behaviour
`` → a behaviour needs a preset; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`Fade-Up` → `Fade-Up` is not a valid preset name; ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade 12x` → unknown token `12x`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade -3f` → `-3f` is not a valid duration; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade 1pxpx` → `1pxpx` is not a valid distance; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade @12` → `@12` is not a valid start time; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade bounce` → unknown curve `bounce`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)
`fade 12f 10f` → duration given twice: `12f` and `10f`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade ease-in cubic(.2,0,0,1)` → curve given twice: `ease-in` and `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `hold`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`

## track
`` → missing the start value in ``; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"
`0 1 @0-5f` → missing `->` after the start value in `0 1 @0-5f`; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"
`0 -> 1` → missing `@<start>-<end>` after the end value in `0 -> 1`; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"
`0 -> 1 2 @0-5f` → missing `@<start>-<end>` after the end value in `0 -> 1 2 @0-5f`; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"
`0 -> 1 @0-5f bouncy` → unknown curve `bouncy`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)
`0 -> 1 @0-5f ease ease` → unexpected `ease` after the curve; expected "<from> -> <to> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out"

## contents
`{"id":"a","shapes":[],"comp":"x"}` → layers[0].comp: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp` or `pivot`; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","pivot":false}` → layers[0].pivot: `pivot` is `true` or left out; expected "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","pivot":true,"fill":"#fff"}` → layers[0].fill: `fill` only applies to `text` or `rect` layers; expected `fill` only next to `text` or `rect`
`{"id":"a","shapes":{}}` → layers[0].shapes: invalid type: map; expected a list of item objects, e.g. [{"rect":[300,100]},{"fill":"#FFE000"}]
`{"id":"a","comp":"nowhere"}` → layers[0].comp: unknown composition `nowhere`: the scene has none; expected a composition under "comps", e.g. "comps":{"card":{"size":"600x400","dur":"5s","layers":[]}}
`{"id":"a","pivot":true,"hidden":1}` → layers[0].hidden: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a boolean

## shapes
`1` → layers[0].shapes[0]: invalid type: integer `1`; expected an item object keyed by its kind, e.g. {"rect":[300,100],"round":12} or {"fill":"#FFE000"}
`{}` → layers[0].shapes[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`
`{"round":3}` → layers[0].shapes[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`
`{"rect":[1,1],"fill":"#fff"}` → layers[0].shapes[0].fill: `rect` and `fill` are both kinds; an item has one; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`
`{"rect":[1,1],"size":[2,2]}` → layers[0].shapes[0].size: `size` is the value `rect` holds; expected the size only as the value of `rect`
`{"rect":[1,1],"colour":1}` → layers[0].shapes[0].colour: unknown rect key `colour`; expected one of rect, id, hidden, anim, position, round
`{"rect":[-1,1]}` → layers[0].shapes[0].rect: value -1 is outside 0..; expected a number of at least 0
`{"rect":"wide"}` → layers[0].shapes[0].rect: `wide` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`{"rect":[1,1],"round":-2}` → layers[0].shapes[0].round: value -2 is outside 0..; expected a number of at least 0
`{"group":{}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].group: invalid type: map; expected a list of item objects, e.g. [{"rect":[300,100]},{"fill":"#FFE000"}]
`{"group":[{"rect":[1,1],"cap":"round"}]}` → layers[0].shapes[0].group[0].cap: unknown rect key `cap`; expected one of rect, id, hidden, anim, position, round
`{"stroke":"#000","cap":"pointy"}` → layers[0].shapes[0].cap: unknown stroke cap `pointy`; expected one of butt, round, square
`{"stroke":"#000","cap":1}` → layers[0].shapes[0].cap: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a string
`{"stroke":"#000","miter":0.5}` → layers[0].shapes[0].miter: value 0.5 is outside 1..; expected a number of at least 1
`{"fill":"#fff","id":"Bad"}` → layers[0].shapes[0].id: invalid id `Bad`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"fill":"#fff","id":"f"},{"group":[{"fill":"#000","id":"f"}]}` → layers[0].shapes[1].group[0].id: duplicate item id `f`; expected every item of a layer to have its own id
`{"path":[1,2]}` → layers[0].shapes[0].path: a path is written as a string of path data, not numbers; expected SVG path data with absolute commands, e.g. `M0,0 C10,0 20,10 20,20 L0,20 Z`: `M` once, then `L x,y` or `C x1,y1 x2,y2 x,y`, and `Z` to close
`{"path":"M0,0 Q1,1 2,2"}` → layers[0].shapes[0].path: `M0,0 Q1,1 2,2` has a command other than `L`, `C` or `Z`; expected SVG path data with absolute commands, e.g. `M0,0 C10,0 20,10 20,20 L0,20 Z`: `M` once, then `L x,y` or `C x1,y1 x2,y2 x,y`, and `Z` to close
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":"M0,0 L1,1 -> M0,0 L2,2 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.path: `path` is a path, which a key list animates; expected a list of keys like [[0, 0], ["12f", 1, "ease-out"]]
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":[{"t":0,"v":"M0,0 L1,1"},{"t":5,"v":"M0,0 L1,1 Z"}]}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.path[1]: a path key differs in vertex count or closure from the first key; expected keys whose paths have the same vertices, all open or all closed
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":[{"t":0,"v":"M0,0 L1,1","curve":["ease","ease"]}]}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.path[0].curve: `path` is a path, so one curve eases every vertex together; expected one curve
`{"rect":[1,1],"anim":{"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.opacity: unknown rect property `opacity`; expected one of size, position, round, width, height, x, y
`{"rect":[1,1],"anim":{"width":"0 -> 1 @0-5f","size":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.size: `width` and `size` both animate `size`; expected `size` animated whole, or its components `width`, `height` one at a time
`{"fill":"#fff","anim":{"color":"#000 -> 2,0,0 @0-5f"}}` → layers[0].shapes[0].anim.color: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1

## text
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","style":{"tracking":1}}` → layers[0].style: `style` only applies to `text` layers; expected `style` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","box":[1,1]}` → layers[0].box: `box` only applies to `text` layers; expected `box` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":[]}` → layers[0].style: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of text style keys, e.g. {"tracking":20,"align":"center"}
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"font":"Inter 9"}}` → layers[0].style.font: `font` is set on the layer, not in `style`; expected `font` as a layer key
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"kerning":1}}` → layers[0].style.kerning: unknown style key `kerning`; expected one of font, italic, fill, stroke, stroke-width, paint, tracking, leading, baseline, caps, faux-bold, faux-italic, align, indent-first, indent-start, indent-end, space-before, space-after, auto-leading
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"tracking":"wide"}}` → layers[0].style.tracking: invalid type: string "wide"; expected a number
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"caps":"loud"}}` → layers[0].style.caps: unknown caps `loud`; expected one of normal, small, all, all-small
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"leading":"tall"}}` → layers[0].style.leading: invalid type: string "tall"; expected `auto` or a number of px
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"stroke":[2,0,0]}}` → layers[0].style.stroke: a colour channel is outside 0 to 1; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"stroke-width":-1}}` → layers[0].style.stroke-width: -1 is below 0; expected a number of at least 0
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"faux-bold":"yes"}}` → layers[0].style.faux-bold: invalid type: string "yes"; expected a boolean
`{"id":"a","text":"x","fill":[1,0]}` → layers[0].fill: 2 numbers do not make a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":{}}` → layers[0].runs: invalid type: map; expected a list of style objects, e.g. [{"range":[0,4],"fill":"#FF0000"}]
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"fill":"#FFF"}]}` → layers[0].runs[0]: missing `range`; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[1,1]}]}` → layers[0].runs[0].range: the range must run forward over whole indices; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,2]}]}` → layers[0].runs[0].range: the range ends at 2, past the text's 1 characters; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,0.5]}]}` → layers[0].runs[0].range: the range must run forward over whole indices; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":"0-1"}]}` → layers[0].runs[0].range: invalid type: string "0-1"; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,1],"align":"center"}]}` → layers[0].runs[0].align: `align` cannot be set on a run; expected `align` in `style` or `paragraphs`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{"tracking":3}]}` → layers[0].paragraphs[0].tracking: `tracking` cannot be set on a paragraph; expected `tracking` in `style` or `runs`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{},{}]}` → layers[0].paragraphs: 2 paragraph styles for 1 paragraphs; expected at most one style per paragraph; `\n` ends a paragraph
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{"align":"middle"}]}` → layers[0].paragraphs[0].align: unknown alignment `middle`; expected one of left, right, center, justify-left, justify-right, justify-center, justify-all
`{"id":"a","text":"x","box":[0,10]}` → layers[0].box: a box is a width and a height above zero; expected `[width, height]` in px, both above zero, e.g. `[600, 300]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","box":"wide"}` → layers[0].box: a box is a width and a height above zero; expected `[width, height]` in px, both above zero, e.g. `[600, 300]`

## fonts
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fonts":"fonts","layers":[]}` → fonts: invalid type: string "fonts"; expected a list of font files and folders, e.g. ["fonts/lato"]
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fonts":[3],"layers":[]}` → fonts[0]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string

## effects
`{"rect":[1,1]}` → layers[0].fx[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `fill`
`{"fill":"#fff","opacity":3}` → layers[0].fx[0].opacity: value 3 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"fill":"#fff","rule":"evenodd"}` → layers[0].fx[0].rule: unknown fill key `rule`; expected one of fill, id, hidden, anim, opacity

## comps
`"card":1` → comps.card: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a composition object, e.g. {"size":"600x400","dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`"Card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → comps.Card: invalid composition id `Card`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`"card":{"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → comps.card: missing `size`; expected e.g. "size":"1080x1920"
`"card":{"size":"1x1","layers":[]}` → comps.card: missing `dur`; expected e.g. "dur":"5s"
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s"}` → comps.card: missing `layers`; expected e.g. "layers":[]
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","fps":0,"layers":[]}` → comps.card.fps: must be a number above zero; expected e.g. `30`
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[],"tint":1}` → comps.card.tint: unknown field `tint`; expected one of size, fps, dur, bg, layers
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x"}]}` → comps.card.layers[0]: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp` or `pivot`; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card" or "pivot":true
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x","comp":"card"}]}` → comps.card.layers[0].comp: composition `card` would draw itself through its layers; expected compositions that never lead back to themselves
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x","comp":"b"}]},"b":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"y","comp":"card"}]}` → comps.card.layers[0].comp: composition `card` would draw itself through its layers; expected compositions that never lead back to themselves

## range
`@x-5f` → `@x-5f` is not a valid range; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`@05f` → `@05f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`@0-5` → `@0-5` needs a unit (`f` or `s`) after the end; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`

## span
`x-5f` → `x-5f` is not a valid range; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`05f` → `05f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`0-5` → `0-5` needs a unit (`f` or `s`) after the end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`@0-5f` → `@0-5f` is not a valid range; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit

## serde
`{}` → missing field `key`
`"dim"` → unknown variant `dim`; expected one of on
